# L §5.10 Value, §5.7 (round 10): `priced p` names "the price input p", valued as num CUR (a place's single position,
# tally 1's asset) or num CUR/u (a price per unit, a holding); a text input prices nothing: LOAD-UNIT, "a value of the
# wrong type" (L §8.3).
=== pr.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input val: text
place flat: assets PLN priced val lives 2026-01-01..

ask q: value(flat, 2026-03-01) in PLN law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  val = "x" "own"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-UNIT ...
